  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design and build of a Holland Lounge during the West Africa Agrofood Fair 2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to add value to the local private sector, specifically the local horti- and agri-sector, by organizing a mission to C&#xF4;te d&apos;Ivoire (hereafter CDI) between the 18th and 24th of November 2018. This mission will strengthen and deepen the growing business relations between the Netherlands and CDI and kick-start the development of high-impact PSD projects. The project also further explores the opportunities and leads as presented in the market study on horticulture that was recently published (September 2018). The desired results are:1.	A draft short- and long-term PSD strategy for agri- and horticulture development.2.	Concrete matches between PSD challenges on a local level and successful Dutch businesses and expertise.3.	Concrete leads for follow-up projects and the DDE and RVO programs that are available:&#x2022;	This could be an impact cluster and demonstration project on seeds with the possibility of a Knowledge to Knowledge (K2K) project with linked and partnered universities.&#x2022;	This could also be a value chain project (DGGF and either CBI or combi) on tropical fruits with the necessary Technical Support and Government to Government (G2G) elements on bottlenecks concerning quality, phytosanitary or customs.&#x2022;	Supporting G2G and K2K projects 4.	Ivorian small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) have learned from Dutch knowledge, expertise and solutions regarding (agro-logistic) challenges they face in their businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
